  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nHigh pressure rebuilding over the region will return a slight \nwarming and drying trend Sunday through Monday, with peak \ndaytime temperatures expected to hover in the lower 80s for the \nTreasure Valley area. Late Monday through Tuesday, the area will\nbe sandwiched between a shortwave trough steering across the \nlower Great Basin and a longwave Pacific trough moving into the \nnorthwest coast. This pattern will keep us in moderated zonal \nflow aloft on Tuesday, with seasonable conditions and a chance \nof showers near the ID-NV border. Come Wednesday, the area will\ncome under a strong southwest flow ahead of the approaching \nPacific trough, continuing dry conditions and temperatures 5 to \n10 degrees above normal through Thursday.",
